On wasip1, a filesystem path that no WASI preopen covers ends buf's
workspace walk instead of failing it.

Reason: buf opens a bucket at the filesystem root and walks up from the
input directory to "/" looking for buf.yaml and buf.work.yaml. slicc-kernel
and SLICC's realm preopen "." and each top-level directory (/home, /tmp,
/dev, …) but not "/" itself, so Go's wasip1 port answers stat("/") and
stat("/buf.yaml") with EBADF, and every module command fails with
"stat /: Bad file number". Preopening "/" in the runtimes breaks wasi-libc
programs' relative paths, so buf works around it. On wasip1 only:
- newBucket accepts "/" when stat fails with EBADF, ENOTCAPABLE or ENOENT;
- validateExternalPath reports such paths as not existing, so the walk
  finds no workspace there and stops.
Other platforms are unchanged (outsidePreopens is false).

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: the runtimes offer an opt-in root preopen for Go programs.

